            <title>0.27.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:56:07 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>60</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.27.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:0;padding:2px 4px}h3{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 4px}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}}</style><h3>What's new in Keeploop 0.27.0</h3><ul><li>Monitors can now carry routes, short labels like duet:my-channel. An AI session that was not open when a monitor was set can call check_route with that label to get the new matches of every monitor that carries it. Part of Pro. A monitor's routes show in Settings &gt; Monitors.</li><li>Web and phone AI apps can now rename a monitor, pause or resume it, change when it ends and change its routes, if they may set monitors. Changing what a monitor watches or how it alerts you is still done only from your Mac.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
