        <item>
            <title>0.26.1</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:51:51 +0200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>59</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.26.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:0;padding:2px 4px}h3{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 4px}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}}</style><h3>What's new in Keeploop 0.26.1</h3><ul><li>Security: the Keeploop service that connects your AI apps, alerts and Slack now refuses certificates from the eMudhra certificate authorities whose keys were compromised (disclosed October 20). Update now.</li><li>Monitors an AI app set in Claude Code keep working after you resume that chat.</li><li>Corrections to the 0.26.0 notes: without Pro or a trial, web and phone AI apps that use Keeploop's connection service cannot list your follow-ups. A reply draft can still be filed under the wrong email when the original has no Message-ID; sending is always checked.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
